    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d161">

                <pb facs="0349" n="249" xml:id="pg249"/>

                <head>No. 161.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Seward to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-04-07"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 7, 1880</date>.
                        (Received June 8.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 654.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Recurring to my dispatch No. 643, in regard
                    to the proposed tax on cargo-boats, I have now the honor to inform you that the
                    subject was considered at a meeting of the diplomatic body held yesterday, and
                    that the several officers present agreed to write to the Yamên, in terms of the
                    note which I inclose herewith.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GEORGE F. SEWARD.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d161-a1.xml" xpointer="d161-a1"/>
            </div>
